<article class="env-definition" id="0CCN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CCN">Definition <span data-tag="0CCN">53.3.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme of dimension $\leq 1$ over $k$. Let $d \geq 0$ and $r \geq 0$. A <em>linear series of degree $d$ and dimension $r$</em> is a pair $(\mathcal{L}, V)$ where $\mathcal{L}$ is an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of degree $d$ (Varieties, Definition <a href="/tag/0AYR" data-tag="0AYR">33.44.1</a>) and $V \subset H^0(X, \mathcal{L})$ is a $k$-subvector space of dimension $r + 1$. We will abbreviate this by saying $(\mathcal{L}, V)$ is a <em>$\mathfrak g^ r_ d$</em> on $X$. </p>
</article>